//SUANN Specification (prompts):

---
add boolean option called trainSetLossOptimisation in both a) the independent benchmark code (population_pertubation_train_convergence_full) and b) LREANNpt populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations code, that controls whether the optimisation of training iterations uses train set loss (trainSetLossOptimisation=True) or validation set loss (trainSetLossOptimisation=False):
	option if(trainSetLossOptimisation==True) must replicate the original behaviour exactly before the validation set upgrade was introduced.
	option if(trainSetLossOptimisation==False) must replicate the new behaviour after the validation set upgrade was introduced.
ensure that the final REPORT prints the final train-set and final validation-set accuracy for all datasets and perturbation population sizes (including standard backprop adam), not just final test-set accuracy.
ensure that the final REPORT prints the total train times for all datasets and perturbation population sizes (including standard backprop adam).
update the population_pertubation_train_convergence_full report generated time table to average the run times across each set of 3 seeds.

---
create delete_population_pertubation_train_convergence_data.py script - resets the folder for a fresh benchmark (removes all files created by the scripts and only leaves the necessary script files to start benchmark from scratch).
update clean_population_pertubation_train_convergence_data.py script - creates a compact results archive.

---
update the git repo codebase to use the bank-full dataset instead of bank in all places (LREANNpt/LREANNpt and LREANNpt/population_pertubation_train_convergence_full)

---
add experimental benchmark population_pertubation_train_convergence_full - conduct thorough benchmark of useStochasticUpdates:usePopulationPertubation=True vs useStochasticUpdates=False, for all populationPertubationPopulationSize (e.g. 64, 256, 1024, 4096). Table your final results after training (test set accuracy), and graph your results in a similar format to populationPertubationExpectedPerformanceGraph.png. Once you have completed this and are satisfied that usePopulationPertubation performance is competitive with backprop, perform benchmarks on all different datasetName. For each dataset, continue their training until they reach optimal train-set performance.
implement option populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations within context if(populationPertubationOptimiseTrainingIterations), which mirrors the current experimental benchmark requirement (population_pertubation_train_convergence_full) of optimising the number of training iterations before evaluating the test set, instead of training a fixed number of repeats/epochs.

---
patch ANNpt_data - fix tabular preprocessing to reuse training-derived normalization and categorical mappings across splits while excluding targets from feature conversion.

---
replace the inaccessible Hugging Face Titanic source with OpenML and prepare numeric predictors and survival labels for training.

